{
  "_note": "Edge types that are the inverse of each other. i3X 1.0 requires every relationship type to register exactly one reverseOf. Where both directions are authored (in two profiles), they must be registered here as a pair, so the two sides cannot drift apart. Checked by ci/lint-edge-pairs.mjs.",
  "pairs": [
    [
      "EXECUTED_AT",
      "EXECUTES"
    ],
    [
      "PRODUCED_BY",
      "YIELDS"
    ],
    [
      "RESOLVED_BY_RULE",
      "RESOLVES"
    ]
  ],
  "open": [
    {
      "type": "PART_OF",
      "inverseOf": [
        "CONTAINS_SEGMENT",
        "MADE_UP_OF"
      ],
      "reason": "ISA-95 names PART_OF the reverse of MADE_UP_OF (catalogue). Registering the pair would demand both sides on every PART_OF / MADE_UP_OF edge, but the tree edges (Machine PART_OF ProcessCell) and MaterialLot MADE_UP_OF Quant are authored one way only. ProcessSegment PART_OF OperationsDefinition and its reverse CONTAINS_SEGMENT are a derived shortcut through OperationsSegment. Model decision (author the missing sides or let i3X derive them), not made here."
    }
  ],
  "_isa95Note": "isa95: for every edge (type, from label) the B2MML field path that carries it, read from standard/validation/isa95-b2mml.json. forward = the path starts at the from object, reverse = at the to object. extension = ISA-95 has no such link, with the reason. derived = a shortcut through an intermediate object: the legs, each a path of the ISA-95 edge catalogue (standard/validation/isa95-edges.json) with its direction, in walking order from the from object. Checked by lint-isa95 and lint-isa95-edges (i3x-v5).",
